    {
      "week": 30,
      "slug": "two-pan-weight-kits",
      "title": "Two-pan weight kits",
      "idea": "Putting a weight on either pan leads to balanced ternary, unique representations and an optimality bound.",
      "gates": "K-1: compare small totals, initially to 6, with adult help through 13. Grades 2-3: addition to 13 and intervals to 40. Grades 4-5: product counting and an argument covering all placements.",
      "materials": "One card for each available weight, two-pan paper mats and counters. Paper labels represent amounts, not real masses. An equal-arm balance with verified cube bundles is optional.",
      "pretest": "If using a real balance, verify the unit masses and equal arms first; that physical pretest has not been performed.",
