    {
      "week": 31,
      "slug": "hidden-orchard",
      "title": "Hidden orchard",
      "idea": "Exact line of sight on a lattice reveals primitive directions, gcd and the complete blocker count.",
      "gates": "K-1: count to 6 and keep thread straight; coordinates may be spoken. Grades 2-3: across-up coordinates and equal groups. Grades 4-5: common factors, division and proportional steps.",
      "materials": "Thin thread, removable tape, pencils, straightedges and dot grids. Use a clear ruler when thread obscures a dot; avoid pins with young children.",
      "pretest": "Check thread thickness and dot visibility on the actual print. Blocking means exactly collinear ideal points, not nearby thick objects.",
