    {
      "week": 32,
      "slug": "squares-inside-rectangles",
      "title": "Squares inside rectangles",
      "idea": "Largest-square removal preserves common divisors and ends with the largest equal grid-square tile.",
      "gates": "K-1: recognize squares and count side lengths to 12. Grades 2-3: repeated grouping or multiplication. Grades 4-5: factors, subtraction and organized bounded searches.",
      "materials": "Printed grids, pencils, ruler and graph paper; scissors are optional. For K-1 Problem 5, prepare four 3-by-3 squares per child on a matching grid.",
      "pretest": "Test any cutouts against their working grid. Separately scaled diagrams need not fit the same physical square.",
