    {
      "week": 33,
      "slug": "prime-length-necklaces",
      "title": "Prime-length necklaces",
      "idea": "Rotation families at prime length give a counting proof of Fermat's little theorem.",
      "gates": "K-1: recognize two labels, count to 6 and move a start arrow. Grades 2-3: group up to 32 cards. Grades 4-5: product counting, division and reasoning about every prime length.",
      "materials": "Flat face-up ring mats, two types of counters and a movable start arrow. Supplied card sheets support sorting; marking families is a no-cut alternative.",
      "pretest": "Check counters fit the actual ring mats. Keep rings face up: turning is allowed, flipping is not.",
